# Cold-Start Push Tap — Stretched WebView Layout Fix

## Symptom
When the app is **killed** and the user taps a push notification, the WebView opens with a stretched or oversized layout (blue/wrong-height content). Rotating the device and back "fixes" it.

## Root cause
`SystemUiMode.immersiveSticky` is set in `initState()` but only takes effect on the **next frame**. WKWebView starts rendering immediately, calculates viewport dimensions while the status bar + home indicator are **still visible**, and bakes in the wrong height. After rotation iOS forces a full viewport recalculation.

## Full fix — all 4 layers required

### Layer 1: `didChangeMetrics()` rebuilds layout

```dart
@override
void didChangeMetrics() {
  if (mounted) setState(() {});
}
```
Fires when `viewPadding` changes after immersive mode settles, updating safe-area insets.

### Layer 2: settle in the phone's ACTUAL orientation — NO rotation nudge

> ⚠️ **LESSON (do NOT regress):** an earlier version forced a micro-rotation to
> `landscapeLeft` and back to recalc the WKWebView frame. On a portrait phone
> this made a cold-start push link **open sideways and then visibly flip** to
> portrait. Never force a different orientation here.
>
> Instead: enter immersive, wait a short beat so the viewport settles **in the
> current device orientation**, then mount + load. Any residual stretch is
> corrected by Layer 4 (post-load `resize` + one `reload`) — in the same
> orientation, with no flip.

```dart
Future<void> _settleColdViewport() async {
  _applyImmersive();
  // Let immersive settle in the ACTUAL orientation before mounting the WebView.
  await Future.delayed(const Duration(milliseconds: 280));
  if (!mounted) return;
  setState(() => _viewportReady = true);
  await _wv.loadRequest(Uri.parse(widget.url));
}
```

For live (non-cold) rotations, do NOT rotate either — poke the page to reflow
by dispatching `orientationchange`+`resize` a few times as the native frame
settles (see `RoostPortal.didChangeMetrics` → `_pokeReflow`), then re-assert
the inset/zoom injections.

### Layer 3: Deferred WebView mount

Do NOT mount `WebViewWidget` until the viewport is stable. Gate on a `_viewportReady` flag:

```dart
// initState — cold-start branch only:
if (widget.coldStartPush) {
  _settleColdViewport();   // immersive → 280ms settle → mount → load (no rotation)
} else {
  _applyImmersive();
  _viewportReady = true;
  _wv.loadRequest(Uri.parse(widget.url));
}

// build:
if (_viewportReady)
  Padding(padding: safe, child: WebViewWidget(controller: _wv))
else
  const ColoredBox(color: Colors.black),
```

### Layer 4: 800ms post-load resize + reload

```dart
// inside onPageFinished:
Future.delayed(const Duration(milliseconds: 800), () {
  if (!mounted) return;
  setState(() {}); // re-read viewPadding
  _wv.runJavaScript(
    'window.dispatchEvent(new Event("resize"));'
    'if(window.visualViewport) window.visualViewport.dispatchEvent(new Event("resize"));',
  );
  _injectSafeArea(); // re-run viewport-fix JS
  if (widget.coldStartPush && !_coldReloadDone) {
    _coldReloadDone = true;
    _wv.reload(); // force full site re-render with correct viewport
  }
});
```

## How to wire `coldStartPush`

Only pass `coldStartPush: true` from the **native cold-start path** (SceneDelegate URL read via `ColdTapReader`). Normal navigation (returning user, app was backgrounded) does NOT need this treatment:

```dart
// BootScreen / VaultSplash — cold-start branch:
final nativeColdUrl = await ColdTapReader.consumeTapUrl();
if (nativeColdUrl != null) {
  _openContent(nativeColdUrl, coldStart: true); // ← flag
  return;
}
```

## ⚠️ Safe-area pitfall

Do NOT use `EdgeInsets.zero` as viewPadding for cold-start — it removes the bottom home-indicator safe area and hides content underneath it. Always use `MediaQuery.of(context).viewPadding`. After immersive mode settles, `didChangeMetrics` fires and top/bottom padding naturally becomes 0.
